===== Previous independent findings A-05/A-06 and remediation =====
The prior Qwen report warned that the auditor saw AttendanceService.punch accepting a caller-supplied staff ID without the controller authorization context (A-05), and that request/null/ID validation before database access was not visible (A-06). Current API controller binds staff identity from CustomUserDetails and validates owner staff/store ownership. SecurityConfig protects /api/attendance/**. New full-filter anonymous request test with valid CSRF is expected to redirect to login. Punch service now rejects null payload, null/nonpositive staff ID, null/unsupported type before mapper access; unit tests assert mapper has no interactions. A new end-to-end MockMvc integration test uses actual SecurityFilterChain with a CustomUserDetails principal and verifies spoofed IDs are overwritten and only the real isolated staff/store IDs are persisted. The concurrency fixture list now uses ConcurrentLinkedQueue.

